# Every numeric limit in the workspace, in one file. Read by core/hooks/file_law.py
# (Python) and sourced directly by check-line-counts.sh (shell) — same file, one law.
#
# Two levels each, deliberately symmetric: a WARN asks for a look, a BLOCK stops the commit.
# Size is a signal, never a quota to game — see core/SCHEMA.md § Routing depth and locality.

# Lines in one code file.
WARN_LINES=150
BLOCK_LINES=200

# Code files in one directory. Splitting an over-full directory costs one routing hop, so
# the WARN is where a split becomes worth considering and the BLOCK is where the directory
# holds more than one responsibility no matter how you read it. A directory at 8-9 files is
# a warning on purpose: a split saving two table rows does not pay for its hop.
WARN_FILES=7
BLOCK_FILES=10

# Tokens of session context. Not a cap — the context window is far larger. This is where
# the *cost* curve bends: measured 2026-08-13 over 119 sessions / 18,508 turns, a turn at
# 300-400k of context costs $0.21 against $0.07 at 50-100k, and 73% of all spend is paid
# above CTX_WARN. Read by core/hooks/session/context-meter.py, which announces each
# threshold once per session and never blocks.
CTX_WARN=150000
CTX_LOUD=250000
